VALUES
(181, 'Article', 18, 'clamamagazine.com', '1', 'A-new-Permanent-Magnet-Doubly-Fed-Contra-Rotor-Induction-Generator', '', 'A new Permanent Magnet Doubly Fed Contra Rotor Induction Generator', '', 'Wind power, electrical generator, induction generator, permanent magnet generator, contra rotor generator', 'The traditional energy resource is fossile fuel Not only it is limitted but also it should be burned and emits CO2 which warms up the earth A new efficient electrical genertor for application in wind farms proposed This electrical generator has two mechanical input and also is hybrid of permanent magent and induction generators  ', 'The traditional energy resource is fossile fuel Not only it is limitted but also it should be burned and emits CO2 which warms up the earth', 'The other emitted greenhause gases also can causes to hole in ozone which was protection layer against dangrous sun rays', 'The CO2 emitted from these power plants is collected at atomsphere and act like a layer trap the heat in the earth', '', 'The increase in temrature of the earth can cause to abrupt changes in climate pattern and sea levels and it endangers human and animal life In the face of environmental and economic challenges, the use of renewable energy is a sustainable solution to energy needs Derived from the sun, wind, water and biomass, these energy sources offer an essential alternative to traditional fossil fuels, namely oil and coal  They are inexhaustible on a human scale and reduce dependence on fossil fuels, thereby reducing the greenhouse gas emissions responsible for climate change  Indeed, the use of renewable energies instead of fossil fuels helps to mitigate the effects of climate change and to fight global warming In addition, the transition to renewable energy creates many job opportunities in the installation, maintenance and manufacturing of renewable energy technologies It also allows nations to increase their energy independence and boost their economies  Finally, renewable energy promotes the diversification of energy production This reduces the risks associated with volatile fossil fuel prices and supply interruptions In addition, the decentralisation and integration of renewable energy sources at different levels helps to increase the resilience of energy systems', 'The changes in the earth temprature causes the changes in the climate pattern which is dangrous for human life', 'Among renewable energies wind power is suitable candidate as there is a hug amount of wind power available on the earth enough to power all the nations', 'The nuclear power converters invented that converts mass to energy ', 'The mass of heavy materials like Uranium is converted to energy This energy is appeared as heat', 'Solar and watter power proposed ', 'Solar energy is converted via solar panels to electrical energy and in water power water flow energy is converted to electrical energy', 'Wind energy is possible in more location', 'Wind energy is possible almost every where even the places the wind slow high altitude wind is strong enough', 'Nuclear power stations are dangrous as severla explosions reported in nuclear power plans Also, these power stations has enviromental impacts dangrous for biological systems like human', 'The nuclear power plans are danrous as  they are in expose of explosion and also their nuclear trashes is dangrous for environment', 'These nuclear power plans are complicated and very expensive to establish', 'Solar enegry suffers from variation in energy production and water energy conversion not possible everywhere and need hug structural foundation and is costy', 'Solar energy is availble enough everhwere and its solar panels are expensive and this energy is not available at night or cloudy times Water energy also is possible only where rievers, damm,  or sea are available and need costy structures', 'Solar energy is not available at nights and water power also need damm or construction near where enough strong water flow exist', 'These wind power stations lack efficient electrical generators', 'The wind turbines mostly use induction generators that are not efficient and also needs a minim speed of wind to generate electricity', 'Wind energy extraction is hard', 'A new efficient electrical genertor for application in wind farms proposed This electrical generator has two mechanical input and also is hybrid of permanent magent and induction generators  ', '', '', 'This electrical generator is compact and it measn more energy extracted per generator structure weight', 'Because it has two mechanical input, shafts, two wind turbines can be connected to it', '', 'The generator has two shafts because it has two rotors inside of the stators and one shaft is connected to each rotor', 'The permanent magents used in this generator causes this electrical generators generates electricity in low wind speeds', '', 'The generator has two shafts because it has two rotors inside of the stators and one shaft is connected to each rotor', 'This generator, which is an permanent magnet induction generator is a type of electrical generator that operates on the principle of electromagnetic induction. Designed to be used in wind turbines, hydroelectric power plants and other renewable energy installations, it produces mechanical energy from electrical energy. \r\nThis induction generator actually consists of a fixed stator of electrically insulated copper coils and a rotor. These coils are wound around the central axis of the generator in the form of a ring and create a magnetic field as shown in Fig.1. When alternating current is applied to the stator. In addition, the stator contains a rotor made of a soft iron structure and copper conductors connected in a short circuit.  The relative movement of the rotor with respect to the rotating magnetic field created by the stator causes an electromagnetic induction. The changing magnetic field in the stator induces an electric voltage in the rotor conductors which generates electric current when the rotor is connected to an external load.\r\nIt should be noted that the normal operation of convetional induction generators requires their synchronisation with the frequency and voltage of the existing electrical grid. This synchronisation involves the use of control and regulation devices, namely: synchronisation and frequency conversion systems. But in this design there is not need for voltage from grid because there are permanent magnets on the rotors, which will be described, create magnetic field and current.\r\n\r\n', 'The-stator-which-has-several-windings-coils-on-it-creates-a-magnetics-field.png', 'The stator which has several windings coils on it creates a magnetics field', 'There are two rotors in the generators. The first rotor which is a cage type rotor. The shaft is the central part that connects the first rotor to the generator and whose movement is driven by the rotor. In fact, it transmits this rotary motion to the generator to generate electricity.  This rotor has a diameter smaller than the second rotor which will be described. In fact, this rotor is inside of the second rotor rotating in opposite direction of it.', 'The-first-rotor-is-cage-types-rotor-and-the-cage-consisted-for-conductive-bars-fixed-like-a-cage.png', 'The first rotor is cage types rotor and the cage consisted for conductive bars fixed like a cage', 'The second rotor is similar to the first rotor with this difference that not only has conductive bars but also magnet bars as indicated as red color in Fig.3. This cage shaped rotor has a larger diameter compared to the first rotor. It has own shaft which will be the second shaft of the electrical generator and will be second input of mechanical energy to the generator.', 'The-second-rotor-is-caged-shaped-with-conductive-and-also-magentics-bars-and-a-shaft-connected-to-it.png', 'The second rotor is caged shaped with conductive and also magentics bars and a shaft connected to it', 'The first rotor rotates in side of the stator the simplified side view presentation of this rotor inside stator shown in Fig.4 ', 'The-second-rotor-inside-stator-rotating-has-a-shaft-.png', 'The second rotor inside stator rotating has a shaft ', 'The second rotor with larger diameter than first rotor inside the stator rotating. The side view presentation of the generator shown in Fig. 5. As seen the center of the first and the second rotors are center of the stator. Also, cross sectional of  the magnetic bars shown in red circle. The cross sectional of the conductive bars shown in gray color. The two rotors has their own shaft each one is rotated using a separate wind turbines in opposite directions.', 'The-second-and-first-rotors-inside-of-the-stator-rotating-in-opposite-directions.png', 'The second and first rotors inside of the stator rotating in opposite directions', 'As mentioned above, the stator is the fixed part of the induction generator and the rotor is the moving part. In fact, the stator consists of a coil wound around a core, usually made of laminated iron with windings supplied with alternating current at a fixed frequency. In addition, first squirrel cage rotor have a structure in the form of protruding magnetic poles, while the poles of wound rotors are equipped with windings. But the second rotor has perment magnet bars that create constant megntic field. It should be noted that the magnetic field also is created by the stator currents when the rotor is rotating inside the stator. It then induces an electric current in the rotor due to electromagnetic induction.  In addition, the current induced in the first rotor cage and also in the second rotor (because it has also conductive bars) in turn produces a magnetic field opposite to the stator field which generates an electromagnetic torque that sets the rotor in rotation. When the rotor rotates, it generates an electrical voltage in the stator windings. ', 'The-simplified-representation-via-of-the-generator-with-two-rotors-and-turbines.png', 'The simplified representation via of the generator with two rotors and turbines', 'The envelope is the outer structure that houses the generator and protects it from the weather. It is usually made of steel or composite materials and protects it from the outside elements. The shafts are the central parts that connects the rotors to the generator and whose movement is driven by the rotors. In fact, they transmits the rotary motion to the generator to generate electricity.\r\nThe electrical connections allow the generator to be connected to the electrical distribution system or to control devices to regulate the production of electricity. In addition, the cooling system dissipates excessive heat and keeps the generator at a safe operating temperature. As shown the electrical generator terminals connected to capacitors then connected to the electrical grid. This capacitors control the reactive power generated by the generator and keep the voltage of the generator in proper range. There is a control system shown in Fig.7 that controls the frequency of the electrical current of the generator.', 'The-hybird-permanent-magnetc-induction-contra-rotor-generator-drived-by-two-wind-tubines-connected-to-the-grid-.png', 'The hybird permanent magnetc induction contra rotor generator drived by two wind tubines connected to the grid ', '', 'The special feature of a this permanent magnet induction generator with two mechanical inputs is that it can be used in wind turbines to convert wind energy into electrical energy efficiently. This advanced generator consists of two rotor, one stator,  two shafts, electrical connections and a cooling system. Two wind turbines which their blades angles are mirrored to rotate in different direction when wind blows to capture the kinetic energy of the wind and transfer it to the rotor via the two shafts, the rotors are connected to the shafts and rotates with the blades in the wind. \r\nAs the fixed part of the generator, the stator consists of a laminated iron core and copper wire coils wound around it. In fact, the stator coils are placed in such a way as to favor the creation of a stationary magnetic field but magnets of the second rotor also amplify this magnetic field. When the rotors are in motion, its magnetic field of magnets on the second rotor interacts with that of the stator to generate an electric voltage. This generator is compact it means is has high energy to weight ratio.  It generate electricity even in low wind speeds. More importantly, this generator does not need gear box to increase rotational speed of the rotors. Because it has two rotors rotating in opposite direction the relative speed between them at least doubled and eliminated the need to any gear box', 'Due to problem of greenhouse effect of the fossil fuels, there is a focus on the wind energy generation technology to extract more energy efficiently. To extract wind energy efficiently a new hybrid permanent magnet induction contra rotor generator proposed. The generator has two rotors rotating in opposite directions in one stator. Each of the rotors has one shaft totally two shafts the generator has. One wind turbine connected to each shaft. The two wind turbines rotate in opposite direction of each others. The second rotor has magnetic elements that causes magnetic field even at low speed of rotation of rotor causes generation of electricity in stator winding while in conventional induction generators magnetic field is not created in low rotor speeds. Because the there are two rotor rotate in different directions their relative speeds is high and this generator does not need gear box which is heavy and costly reduces the total cost of the generator.', 'Lahcene Ouazene; George McPherson', 'Analysis of the Isolated Induction Generator', 'IEEE Transactions on Power Apparatus and Systems', 'Volume: PAS-102, Issue: 8, August 1983', 'S. Mouty, C. Espanet', '12 - Development of permanent magnet generators to integrate wind turbines into electricity transmission and distribution networks', 'Eco-Friendly Innovation in Electricity Transmission and Distribution Networks', 'Volume: 2, Issue: 9', 'M. Orabi South Valley University, Aswan, Egypt ; T. Ahmed; M. Nakaoka; M.Z. Youssef', 'Efficient performances of induction generator for wind energy', ' 30th Annual Conference of IEEE Industrial Electronics Society, 2004. IECON 2004', 'Volume: 5,1 Issue: 12', 'Samir Jackson, Adam Acuff, Alberta Beare ', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', 0, 0, 1, '', '', '', '', '', '');

